translation:
Target is the proposition that for every type Fm of sentences equipped with the formal logical connectives (implication, conjunction, disjunction, negation) and truth/falsehood constants, every type S of proof systems equipped with a provability relation ⊢ on Fm, every proof system 𝓢 : S that proves all classical propositional tautologies and is closed under modus ponens, every pair of arbitrary functions T, K : Fm → Fm from sentences to sentences, and every six sentences σ, S₀, S', G, P, Q : Fm, if all of the following eight conditions hold:
1. 𝓢 proves σ 🡒 T(σ);
2. K satisfies the rule Def3 for 𝓢, namely that for every sentence φ : Fm, if 𝓢 proves φ then 𝓢 proves K(φ);
3. 𝓢 proves σ 🡒 S₀;
4. 𝓢 proves S₀ 🡒 (T(σ) 🡒 S');
5. 𝓢 proves S' 🡒 G;
6. 𝓢 proves S' 🡒 ∼P;
7. 𝓢 proves Q 🡒 P;
8. 𝓢 proves σ 🡒 (K(σ 🡒 G) 🡒 Q);
then 𝓢 proves ∼σ.

No further assumptions are made: 𝓢 need not be consistent, T and K are arbitrary sentence-to-sentence functions with no other properties assumed (in particular, σ 🡒 T(σ) is only assumed for the specific sentence σ, not for all sentences), and σ, S₀, S', G, P, Q are arbitrary sentences.

